---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BentoCard from '../../components/BentoCard.astro';

const lang = 'en';
---

<style>
	details.thesis-details > summary {
		list-style: none;
		cursor: pointer;
		display: flex;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: 0.375rem;
	}
	details.thesis-details > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}
	details.thesis-details > summary::before {
		content: '▶';
		font-size: 0.55rem;
		margin-top: 0.25rem;
		flex-shrink: 0;
		opacity: 0.4;
		transition: transform 0.2s ease;
	}
	details.thesis-details[open] > summary::before {
		transform: rotate(90deg);
	}
	details.thesis-details > summary:hover::before {
		opacity: 0.7;
	}
</style>

<Layout title="People" lang={lang}>
	<section class="mb-16">
		<h1 class="text-5xl font-black mb-12 tracking-tighter">
			Our <span class="text-intellect font-montserrat italic">People</span>
		</h1>

		<div class="bento-grid">
			<!-- PI Card -->
			<BentoCard class="md:col-span-3 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-10 items-center md:items-start" showBorderBeam={true}>
				<div class="w-full md:w-72 h-72 rounded-xl overflow-hidden flex-shrink-0 border-2 border-intellect/20 shadow-2xl shadow-intellect/10">
					<img src="/images/kien-truong.jpg" alt="Dr. Kien Truong" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
				</div>
				<div class="flex-grow">
					<h2 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-3 tracking-tight">
						Dr. Kien Truong
					</h2>
					<p class="text-intellect font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-8 bg-intellect/10 inline-block px-4 py-1.5 rounded-md">Principal Investigator</p>
					
					<div class="text-contrast/80 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
						<p><strong>Dr. Kien Truong</strong> is currently a Lecturer in the Computer Science Physics Division, Faculty of Physics and Engineering Physics, University of Science, VNU-HCM. He is an IEEE Senior Member and a VEF alumnus.</p>
						<p>He received the M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Electrical Engineering from The University of Texas at Austin (UT Austin) under the supervision of Prof. Robert W. Heath, Jr. His research interests include Massive MIMO, wireless power transfer, and signal processing for 6G networks.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</BentoCard>

			<!-- Current Members -->
			<BentoCard class="md:col-span-3">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-8 tracking-tight flex items-center gap-3">
					<span class="p-2.5 rounded-md bg-insight/10 text-insight">👥</span>
					Current Members
				</h2>
				<div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
					<!-- Cao Khánh Duy -->
					<div class="group p-6 rounded-lg bg-foundation border border-black/5 dark:border-white/5 hover:border-insight/30 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-insight/5 transition-all duration-500">
						<img src="/images/DuyCao.jpeg" alt="Cao Khánh Duy" class="w-full rounded-lg mb-5 object-contain" />
						<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-starlight tracking-tight mb-2">Cao Khánh Duy</h3>
						<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
							<span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-insight bg-insight/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-sm border border-insight/20">22CVD</span>
							<span class="text-xs font-bold text-contrast/50 bg-black/5 dark:bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-sm">Senior Thesis</span>
						</div>
						<div class="pt-4 border-t border-black/5 dark:border-white/5">
							<div>
								<p class="text-xs font-black text-contrast/40 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Project</p>
								<details class="thesis-details">
									<summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-starlight leading-relaxed">Design and implementation of a vision enhancement system on the FPGA DE1-SoC platform</summary>
									<div class="mt-4">
										<p class="text-xs font-black text-contrast/40 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Abstract</p>
										<p class="text-sm text-contrast/70 leading-relaxed">In the context of surveillance and rescue applications requiring precise observation under harsh weather conditions, vision enhancement systems play a critically important role. This thesis focuses on the design and implementation of a real-time dehazing and desmoke system on the FPGA DE1-SoC platform. By optimizing the SoC architecture, tasks are efficiently partitioned between FPGA hardware (parallel DSP processing with low latency via Verilog) and HPS software (system control on ARM Cortex-A9). The workflow from MATLAB simulation and ModelSim verification to Quartus execution demonstrates the superior advantage of FPGAs in high-speed image processing. The research results not only improve real-world image quality but also establish a standard framework for future intelligent vision enhancement systems.</p>
									</div>
								</details>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Nguyễn Thái Hoà -->
					<div class="group p-6 rounded-lg bg-foundation border border-black/5 dark:border-white/5 hover:border-prestige/30 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-prestige/5 transition-all duration-500">
						<div class="w-full h-36 rounded-lg mb-5 bg-gradient-to-br from-prestige/10 to-insight/10 flex items-center justify-center border border-prestige/10 group-hover:from-prestige/15 group-hover:to-insight/15 transition-all duration-500">
							<span class="text-4xl font-black text-prestige/40 tracking-tighter select-none group-hover:text-prestige/60 transition-colors duration-500">NTH</span>
						</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-starlight tracking-tight mb-2">Nguyễn Thái Hoà</h3>
						<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
							<span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-prestige bg-prestige/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-sm border border-prestige/20">22CVD</span>
							<span class="text-xs font-bold text-contrast/50 bg-black/5 dark:bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-sm">Senior Thesis</span>
						</div>
						<div class="pt-4 border-t border-black/5 dark:border-white/5">
							<div>
								<p class="text-xs font-black text-contrast/40 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Project</p>
								<details class="thesis-details">
									<summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-starlight leading-relaxed">Multi-physics simulation of liquid-metal reconfigurable antenna systems</summary>
									<div class="mt-4">
										<p class="text-xs font-black text-contrast/40 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Abstract</p>
										<p class="text-sm text-contrast/70 leading-relaxed">Liquid-metal antenna systems are attracting significant interest in the development of sixth-generation (6G) mobile networks due to their flexible reconfigurability in geometric structure and radiation characteristics. This thesis focuses on the radiation patterns and characteristic performance parameters of liquid-metal antenna arrays through full-wave electromagnetic simulation using the Electromagnetic Waves, Frequency Domain interface in COMSOL Multiphysics. The results provide a detailed analysis of the impact of parameters such as element count, geometric configuration, and operating frequency on key performance metrics including gain and return loss. These findings not only offer deep insight into the electromagnetic behavior of liquid-metal antennas, but also establish a foundational simulation framework for future fluid-based reconfigurable antenna systems.</p>
									</div>
								</details>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Nguyễn Thiên Nhi -->
					<div class="group p-6 rounded-lg bg-foundation border border-black/5 dark:border-white/5 hover:border-intellect/30 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-intellect/5 transition-all duration-500">
						<img src="/images/NguyenThienNhi.jpg" alt="Nguyễn Thiên Nhi" class="w-full rounded-lg mb-5 object-contain" />
						<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-starlight tracking-tight mb-2">Nguyễn Thiên Nhi</h3>
						<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
							<span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-intellect bg-intellect/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-sm border border-intellect/20">23CVD</span>
							<span class="text-xs font-bold text-contrast/50 bg-black/5 dark:bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-sm">Senior Thesis</span>
						</div>
						<div class="pt-4 border-t border-black/5 dark:border-white/5">
							<div>
								<p class="text-xs font-black text-contrast/40 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Project</p>
								<details class="thesis-details">
									<summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-starlight leading-relaxed">Design and implementation of image processing cores on FPGA for target color recognition and path detection for navigation</summary>
									<div class="mt-4">
										<p class="text-xs font-black text-contrast/40 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Abstract</p>
										<p class="text-sm text-contrast/70 leading-relaxed">This project focuses on researching, optimizing algorithmic architectures, and implementing real-time image processing IP cores using hardware description languages (or High-Level Synthesis - HLS tools). Specific technical tasks include designing a color space conversion core (RGB to YCbCr conversion using fixed-point arithmetic optimized for hardware resources); designing an image segmentation core (target or lane identification based on color thresholding and binary conversion); designing a Sobel edge detection core (constructing a spatial convolution filter to extract edges from grayscale images as a precursor to the Hough transform); designing a path extraction core using Hough transform (designing a parallel computing architecture using trigonometric look-up tables and an optimized buffer to store the accumulator matrix using M10K memory blocks); and optimizing the processing pipeline to synchronize with the input video stream rate. The resulting hardware-optimized IP cores can operate independently or integrate directly via a Streaming interface into the main hardware system for object recognition and navigation assistance.</p>
									</div>
								</details>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</BentoCard>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
